From: Octo <180629317+OctoAlgo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:42:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 29/39] Host heap slots behind striped locks
 (VICTORY_MADE_STRIPES; 1 = one lock as before)

The host heap's `made` keys move from one Mutex<Vec<u64>> to one atomic key
per slot behind N striped locks (descriptor/slots.rs, no Windows types: its
tests run natively). With VICTORY_MADE_STRIPES=1 (default) every slot is
behind the same lock, as before. With 1024, the heap sync on the submitting
thread, the pass over buffer views on a recording thread and the title's
view calls stop waiting for each other slot by slot, and a slot whose key is
already the record's is answered from the atomic without any lock.

Rules: a slot's descriptor is written before its key, under its stripe; a
stale slot of another stripe is made null after the held stripe is released
and only if its key is still the one seen (Made::change_if), so two threads
never take two stripes in opposite orders. `kept` becomes one lock per slot.

